00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.280
Jack: A Backend developer is a person
who builds and maintains the technology

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.010
needed for to make sure that data or
services requested by the front end

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.260
system or software, are delivered.

00:00:11.259 --> 00:00:15.000
They use their understanding of
programming languages and tools to solve

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.050
problems and their responsibilities may
involve creating, maintaining, testing,

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.490
and debugging the ‘back end’ which allows
the software or hardware to function.

00:00:25.509 --> 00:00:29.029
To be a Backend developer it is
often a requirement to have a BA in

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:33.120
computer science or another closely
related field and have worked their

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.560
way up from a more junior role.

00:00:35.369 --> 00:00:39.690
Backend developers need good technological
skills and are often well versed in

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.590
several different programming languages.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.650
See below to learn more about this role.

